effects_from:
ZzzCharacter.cpp's per-frame effect switch, where MODEL_CHAIN_SCORPION shares a case with MODEL_DARK_KNIGHT and MODEL_LARVA - and where MODEL_BUDGE_DRAGON's case above it runs on into the same lines, having no break:

    if (c->Dead == 0 && rand_fps_check(4))
        ... CreateParticle(BITMAP_SMOKE + 1, Position, o->Angle, Light);

with Position scattered 32 units about its feet and BITMAP_SMOKE rather than SMOKE + 1 in Devias alone. That is exactly the Budge Dragon's ground_dust, so it is declared the same way and drawn by the same Dust; it stops when the animal dies, as the gate says.

sprites_from:
The same case, before the dust:

    Vector(0.f, 0.f, 0.f, p);
    b->TransformPosition(o->BoneTransform[7], p, Position, true);
    Vector(Luminosity * 1.f, Luminosity * 0.4f, Luminosity * 0.2f, Light);
    CreateSprite(BITMAP_LIGHT, Position, 1.f, Light, o);

Bone 7 is light_point, on the tip of the tail, with no offset. BITMAP_LIGHT is Effect/flare01.jpg, a 64-square white star, at scale 1: 64 units across. The Light is an orange, and Luminosity is the one MoveCharacterVisual rolls once per frame before the switch - `(float)(rand() % 8 + 2) * 0.1f`, one of eight steps from 0.2 to 0.9 - so the sting gutters like a coal rather than pulsing like an eye. Rolled at MU's 25 a second rather than per drawn frame; see Shaders.Glint.
